Z||000000||Monkeyman||05-17-2000||01:33 PM||||Actually, I hate "Lockworks".  It took Autozone almost a week to get my new door lock cylinders in.  I finally started to install them this am (pass side was fairly easy, but the drivers side wasn't).  I was having some trouble with the drivers side so it was taking me a while.  (A little bit of sweat and a whole lotta frustration.)  Just when I thought I had it done, the d*** lock cylinder fell apart! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">  Can you believe that S***!   Now I have to remove the pass side door panel, etc to take that one out so I can install another set whenever they get in!  4 hours wasted! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">  I did, however, get smart and drill out one of the rivets holding the ?support? bar on the door.  At least I can get my hand in there now.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><BR>Thanx for letting me vent.  I'll be alright (maybe).<P>Here's a problem, though.  For some reason, I couldn't seem to get the horseshoe shaped retainer to go around the cylinder the right way.  I guess it was going in front of where it was supposed to go.  Any suggestions??  I'd like to avoid some of the frustration when  I try this again.  BTW, I have p/locks so the actuator is sort of in the way of my hands.||||reg||8
